.TH "RAPTOR-REGISTER-FILE-TYPES" 1 "2026-10" "RAPTOR Studio" "RAPTOR Studio Manual"
.SH NAME
raptor\-register\-file\-types \- open .rbds and .rbd files with RAPTOR Studio (this user only)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBraptor register\-file\-types\fR [\-h] [\-\-unregister] [\-\-force] [\-\-dry\-run]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Associate .rbds and .rbd model files with RAPTOR Studio for the current user, so double\-clicking one opens it: for a pip or venv install, which has no installer to do it. .rbd is Raptor 7's extension: it is left alone when another program already opens it, unless \-\-force.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Options
.TP
\fB\-\-unregister\fR
undo the registration
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
take .rbd even when another program opens it
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
list the changes without making them
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBraptor\fR(1)
